WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.410
Hi! After ninety-nine, we need hundreds. Today we'll learn numbers up to 1000, with hundreds, tens and ones.

2
00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.882
Three hundred and forty-six has 3 hundreds, 4 tens and 6 ones.

3
00:00:16.032 --> 00:00:21.810
From the right, the first place is ones, the second is tens, and the third is hundreds.

4
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:26.346
10 ones make 1 ten, and 10 tens make 1 hundred.

5
00:00:26.496 --> 00:00:30.618
10 hundreds make one thousand.

6
00:00:30.768 --> 00:00:35.082
Read from the biggest place: three hundred and forty-six.

7
00:00:35.232 --> 00:00:40.074
In 508 the tens place is 0: five hundred and eight.

8
00:00:40.224 --> 00:00:45.210
In 720 the ones place is 0: seven hundred and twenty.

9
00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:51.186
When writing, if a place has nothing, write 0 to hold the place.

10
00:00:51.336 --> 00:00:55.794
Watch out! Five hundred and eight is not 58!

11
00:00:55.944 --> 00:01:02.322
It has 5 hundreds, 0 tens and 8 ones, so we write 0 in the tens place.

12
00:01:02.472 --> 00:01:07.506
So it's 508, a 3-digit number.

13
00:01:07.656 --> 00:01:17.010
Your turn! In 472, which place is the 7 in? Pause and think.

14
00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:25.410
The 7 is in the tens place. It means 7 tens, which is 70. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:35.466
Another one! What number is 6 hundreds, 0 tens and 9 ones? Pause and think.

16
00:01:35.616 --> 00:01:41.682
It's 609, six hundred and nine. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:41.832 --> 00:01:50.346
Here's another! How do we write eight hundred and thirty? Pause and think.

18
00:01:50.496 --> 00:01:58.554
8 hundreds, 3 tens and 0 ones: 830. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:58.704 --> 00:02:07.098
Try one more! How do we read 405? Pause and think.

20
00:02:07.248 --> 00:02:12.450
It's four hundred and five. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:20.610
Try one more! What do 10 hundreds make? Pause and think.

22
00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:27.210
10 hundreds make one thousand, 1000. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:37.266
Try one more! What number is 4 hundreds, 0 tens and 9 ones? Pause and think.

24
00:02:37.416 --> 00:02:45.018
The tens digit is 0: 409, four hundred and nine. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:45.168 --> 00:02:55.770
Last one! Which is greater, 638 or 683? Pause and think.

26
00:02:55.920 --> 00:03:05.610
Same hundreds; compare tens: 3 is less than 8, so 683 is greater. Did you get it right?

27
00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:15.786
Remember: 3-digit numbers have hundreds, tens and ones. Read from the biggest place. When writing, put 0 in an empty place.

28
00:03:15.936 --> 00:03:21.161
Find some 3-digit numbers at home and read them aloud!

